\par\b\fs28 A2. Connecting hypotheses\b0\fs24\par


\par Hypothesis 1 (one axis): the centre is receiving vs grasping alone \u8212? creation as gift, fall as grasp.\par


\par Hypothesis 2 (relation): the centre is Source \u8596? Trajectory \u8212? the creating word that also remains (Matt. 24:35), from \u8220?in the beginning\u8230? and God said\u8221? to \u8220?my words shall not pass,\u8221? with gift, grasp, death and grace along the way.\par


\par Which explains the most data with the least strain? Hypothesis 2. It explains why the lights (1:14) and the new moon (haftarah) and their going-out (Matt. 24) cohere, and why the ending is grace (6:8). Hypothesis 1 leaves haftarah and gospel dangling.\par


\par What would refute this reading? If the word did not return as a constant (Matt. 24:35) and the lights/new moon played no part, the weight would lie with the one axis.\par



