\par\b\fs28 A4. Movement\b0\fs24\par


\par What is unmasked? The grasp: taking what you were given to receive, wanting to be as God apart from the Giver (3:6) \u8212? the primal form of all evil, and trusting in the made which passes away.\par


\par What frame does the text put in its place? The creating word that is gift and remains: receive the world from His hand, and hang your life on the word that does not pass away (Matt. 24:35).\par


\par What concrete response and formation follow? Receiving again instead of grasping; leaving the appointed times to the Father (the hour He alone knows); and abiding in the Word, even when the lights go out.\par


\par \b Core sentence:\b0  God spoke and it was; man grasped and death came; but grace was found \u8212? and the word that created remains as heaven and earth pass away.\par


\par \b Horizon (ground, not the week\u8217?s theme):\b0  the creating word became flesh in Yeshua (John 1:14) and \u8220?my words shall not pass away\u8221? (Matt. 24:35) \u8212? confessional horizon, not peshat-setter.\par


